      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to analyze the pattern and determine the number of toothpicks required for the 250th stage.\n\n1. **Count the number of toothpicks in the first few stages:**\n   - Stage 1: We have 4 toothpicks.\n   - Stage 2: We add 3 more toothpicks, so we have \\(4 + 3 = 7\\) toothpicks.\n   - Stage 3: We add another 3 toothpicks, so we have \\(7 + 3 = 10\\) toothpicks.\n   - In general, for stage \\(n\\), we have \\(4 + 3(n-1)\\) toothpicks.\n\n2. **Find the expression for the number of toothpicks in the \\(n\\)-th stage:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of toothpicks in the } n\\text{-th stage} = 4 + 3(n-1) = 4 + 3n - 3 = 3n + 1\n   \\]\n\n3. **Substitute \\(n = 250\\) into the expression to find the number of toothpicks in the 250th stage:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of toothpicks in the 250th stage} = 3 \\times 250 + 1 = 750 + 1 = 751\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of toothpicks necessary to create the arrangement for the 250th stage is \\(\\boxed{751}\\).",
