      "text": "To determine how many toothpicks are necessary to create the arrangement for the 250th stage, we start by understanding the pattern of toothpicks added at each stage. The first three stages show:\n\n1. **Stage 1:** \\(1\\) toothpick\n2. **Stage 2:** \\(3\\) toothpicks\n3. **Stage 3:** \\(3 + 3 = 6\\) toothpicks\n\nIn general, at each stage, \\(3\\) toothpicks are added to the previous arrangement. This means that by the \\(n\\)-th stage, the total number of toothpicks used can be expressed as an arithmetic series where the first term \\(a_1 = 1\\) and the common difference \\(d = 3\\).\n\nThe \\(n\\)-th term of an arithmetic series is given by:\n\\[\na_n = a_1 + (n-1)d\n\\]\nFor the 250th stage, \\(n = 250\\):\n\\[\na_{250} = 1 + (250-1) \\cdot 3\n\\]\n\\[\na_{250} = 1 + 249 \\cdot 3\n\\]\n\\[\na_{250} = 1 + 747\n\\]\n\\[\na_{250} = 748\n\\]\n\nThus, the number of toothpicks necessary to create the arrangement for the 250th stage is \\(\\boxed{748}\\).",
